# Greta, Sweettooth Scourge: "When Greta enters, create a Food token." and "{G}, Sacrifice a Food: Put a +1/+1 counter on target
# creature. Activate only as a sorcery." Turn 1: Greta is paid by Jet's {B}, the Forest's {G} and Pearl's {1}, so Emerald and Ruby stay
# untapped; the ETB makes the Food. During Bot2's turn 2, in its end step, the ability is refused though the Food, Emerald's {G} and a
# creature (Bot1's Memnite) are all there (sorcery speed, CR 307.5). Turn 3: the Mox Ruby, an artifact but no creature, is not a legal
# target; then Emerald's {G} alone pays, the Food token is sacrificed and Bot1's Memnite gets the counter (2/2); the pool is empty
# afterwards, so the cost is exactly {G}.

